{"model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","input":["What receiving record ties the restored museum loan to its handoff details?","The restored maritime exhibit is packed in crate MEX-2047.","The courier contact for crate MEX-2047 is Northline Art Logistics.","Crate MEX-2047 is received at the east loading dock before the gallery handoff.","museum exhibit shipping: the insurance binder is filed under the winter loan archive.","museum exhibit shipping: the registrar checks frame corners during an unrelated intake.","museum exhibit shipping: the gallery lights use a separate evening inspection schedule.","museum exhibit shipping: the packing room keeps spare foam on the lower shelf.","museum exhibit shipping: the visitor desk prints a separate accessibility map.","museum exhibit shipping: the conservation team logs humidity beside the north wall.","museum exhibit shipping: the education room stores a duplicate lesson kit.","museum exhibit shipping: the courier calendar reserves a different sculpture window.","museum exhibit shipping: the archive scanner uses a separate accession profile.","museum exhibit shipping: the security desk records an unrelated alarm test.","museum exhibit shipping: the donor office sends a separate receipt packet.","museum exhibit shipping: the loading crew labels empty pallets after closing."],"truncate":false}